[sigma@pawl.rpi.edu (Kevin J Martin) writes:]
{{{ in response to a bug report involving a filename prefix "Huh?" }}}
[] I don't know the details of MacOS, but is it possible that ? is a wildcard
[] in the same fashion as ? and * on MSDOS and *nix?  Attempting to create or
[] otherwise directly access any file with a wildcard in its name will cause
[] a file creation error on such systems.  This could be your problem.
[] I suppose a fix in terms of Nethack code would be to disallow anything but
[] alphanumerics, - and ' in character names...?

To some extent the game does this. However, on both VAX/Unix and the mac
I play a character called "Spy?" with no problems related to the "?".
To my knowledge, the only reserved character for mac filenames is ":",
which delimits files/folders. In fact, most mac filenames regularly have
spaces as part of the filename. Also on unix, you can quote most of the
wildcards and special characters to avoid problems.

Barry's problem may, in fact, not be related to disk space. The situation
is under investigation (i.e. I've tried to recreate the error message with
various results).

